`self.splits` is determined in `__init__`: with `main_pane="left"` and `clockwise=True`, the split cycle is left, top, right, bottom. In `get_spiral`, `main_pane_ratio` is `None`, so every split uses `self.ratio = 0.71`, and each split function truncates with `int(...)`. Starting from `(23, 47, 1621, 941)`, the code repeatedly splits the remaining rectangle and appends the produced window. When the next candidate window becomes too small under `has_invalid_size`—which compares width/height against margins `[9, 14, 6, 12]` plus `2 * border_width`—the method appends the current remaining rectangle and stops. That produces these seven rectangles.

